# Codebase discovery

**Why:** Random file reads waste tokens and miss how modules connect.

## Before big changes

1. If `.understand-anything/knowledge-graph.json` exists — use for structure/domains (read summaries; no auto `/understand` from MCP).
2. Else `graphify update . --wiki` when CLI available; read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md`.
3. Use `graphify query` for targeted structural questions.
4. Read `devkit://handbook/agents/codebase-discovery.md`, `devkit://graphify-workflow`, and optionally `devkit://understand-anything-workflow`.

## After edits

`graphify update .` to refresh the AST map. Do not run Understand Anything’s LLM pipeline unless the user requests it.

## When neither graph exists

Read one feature folder end-to-end before spreading changes.

## MCP

- `project_intelligence` for scripts/deps/git status
- `safe-run` with `graphify` when allowed
